---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons backup restore -h <==
Restore the whole WTF/ (keybindings, macros, every addon's settings) from a backup, or with --addon
one addon's settings (undoable)

Usage: omaddons backup restore [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>
          The backup: its id, or a prefix of 8 or more characters

Options:
      --addon <ADDON>
          Only this addon's settings (repeatable): its name, ref or a folder; folder:<F> for one
          folder alone

Global options:
      --json
          One JSON envelope on stdout

      --robot
          The same as --json

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format
          
          [possible values: json, human]

  -t, --target <TARGET>
          The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the Classic Era client),
          family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every client)
          
          [alias: --flavor]

      --dry-run
          Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change nothing)

      --actor <ACTOR>
          Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]

      --reason <TEXT>
          Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by commands that change
          nothing)

      --offline
          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]

      --while-running
          Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)

      --if-match <TOKEN>
          Change nothing unless the plan is still the one the --dry-run that returned this token
          (data.precondition) showed

      --no-color
          No ANSI color

      --no-progress
          No progress output

      --progress <MODE>
          Progress events on stderr
          
          [possible values: json, human, none]

      --quiet
          Only errors on stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          More detail (repeatable)

  -h, --help
          Show help

Examples:
  omaddons backup restore 01M6Q2VA --dry-run   what it would put back, and its token
  omaddons backup restore 01M6Q2VA -t retail
  omaddons backup restore 01M6Q2VA -t retail --addon WeakAuras   one addon's settings
  omaddons undo                                put back what it replaced

Restores the whole WTF/ (keybindings, macros, chat and every addon's settings) as the
backup holds them; use --addon for one addon: only the SavedVariables of the folders it
had when the backup was taken, under every account and character. It refuses while the
game runs (or may be running), and where files cannot be replaced in one atomic step; it
checks the copy against the backup's hashes when it has them. Before a whole restore,
where the filesystem clones files, it keeps the current WTF/ as a backup (before
restore), and undo puts back what a restore replaced either way.
--if-match <token> restores exactly what that --dry-run showed.
